nput files, it seems worth considering.  I suppose the main decision is whether it's common enough that adding another option is worth it to avoid a workaround---either the abuse of --outputs you mention or a command like \"datalad unlock {inputs} \u0026\u0026 \u003cregular command\u003e\".\n\nThis touches a separate issue (related to issues #2276 and #2454) of how `run` should consider deleted files, which don't nicely fit into the concept of an output.  From a technical point of view, though, your currently failing example should succeed with datalad-revolution's rev-save (and quickly testing, it does).  Not worth much, but without rev-save, this particular example could avoid #2454 by using gunzip's --keep.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1544454758,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE2MDYzNTQ4MA=="},"target":"047f63dcff447e7c1f17fc71011bca8f7e8f1f00cdc1c10d0f0dcb72357cae77","message":"\u003e but I wonder if it is worthwhile adding an option to run to unlock also input files?\n\nGiven that some tools have issues dealing with symlinked input files, it seems worth considering.  I suppose the main decision is whether it's common enough that adding another option is worth it to avoid a workaround---either the abuse of --outputs you mention or a command like `datalad unlock {inputs} \u0026\u0026 \u003cregular command\u003e`.\n\nThis touches a separate issue (related to issues #2276 and #2454) of how `run` should consider deleted files, which don't nicely fit into the concept of an output.  From a technical point of view, though, your currently failing example should succeed with datalad-revolution's rev-save (and quickly testing, it does).  Not worth much, but without rev-save, this particular example could avoid #2454 by using gunzip's --keep.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1544496046,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NjA1MTYxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3081#issuecomment-446051616"},"message":"Just FTR, for `gzip`, a good enough workaround seems to be adding `-f` (`--force`) option. heh heh.\nSome other tools from my memory which are very touchy with symlinks and require some other workarounds are AFNI, so I wouldn't be surprised if @afni folks eventually come about with some requests like this.  but otherwise I am ok to have this one closed until we run into a similar need again.\n\nindeed on a quick try rev-run performs better (I do need to list --outputs identical to inputs to have the deletion saved though in --explicit mode)","files":null}]}